.TH CWE-401 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-401 \- Missing Release of Memory after Effective Lifetime
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not sufficiently track and release allocated memory after it has been used, which slowly consumes remaining memory. This is often triggered by improper handling of malformed data or unexpectedly interrupted sessions. In some languages, developers are responsible for tracking memory allocation and releasing the memory. If there are no more pointers or references to the memory, then it can no longer be tracked and identified for release.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2023\-26083
Arm Mali Graphics Processing Unit (GPU), added 2023\-04\-07.
.PP
Arm Mali GPU Kernel Driver Information Disclosure Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Arm Mali GPU Kernel Driver contains an information disclosure vulnerability that allows a non\-privileged user to make valid GPU processing operations that expose sensitive kernel metadata.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2023\-04\-28.
.PP
